/// The flocking rules' settings. Each rule has a weight (how hard it
/// steers) and a radius (how far a boid looks for it). viewAngle is the
/// field of view in degrees, centered on the heading: 180 sees only ahead,
/// 360 sees all around. Separation ignores it; you feel a bump from behind.
///
/// Clear view and back off split the fourth rule from Gary William
/// Flake's "The Computational Beauty of Nature" (1998). Both react to
/// blockers, boids closer than blockerRadius inside a cone straight
/// ahead, blockerCone degrees wide. Clear view steps sideways out from
/// behind them; back off steps away from them. Flake's rule is mostly
/// back off with a little clear view. Both are off (weight 0) by default.
type Rules
  cohesion:         Double
  alignment:        Double
  separation:       Double
  cohesionRadius:   Double
  alignmentRadius:  Double
  separationRadius: Double
  viewAngle:        Double
  clearView:        Double
  backOff:          Double
  blockerRadius:    Double
  blockerCone:      Double

/// the original settings: see only ahead, barely any separation, and
/// the blocker rules off (the blocker radius and cone are Flake's)
constructor Rules default -> Rules = Rules
  cohesion:           0.01
  alignment:          0.05
  separation:         0.001
  cohesionRadius:    50.0
  alignmentRadius:   50.0
  separationRadius:   5.0
  viewAngle:        180.0
  clearView:          0.0
  backOff:            0.0
  blockerRadius:     40.0
  blockerCone:       90.0
